cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PseudoPath in your research, please cite this software using these
  metadata.
type: software
title: PseudoPath
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  PseudoPath is a Python package for detecting identifying entities in clinical
  text. It combines fixed rules adapted from EDS-Pseudo with a configurable
  named-entity recognition model and a trained residual line router.
  Recall-calibrated routing presets balance detection quality and CPU
  throughput. The package supports model training, custom model integration,
  spaCy span predictions, and saving and loading trained pipelines.
